{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Precious</b> — He stated the reason why HaShem delivered him: because he is among the pious." "<b>Precious</b> — It means \"heavy,\" as in <i>the price of redeeming a life is heavy</i>. It is hard in the eyes of HaShem to put His pious ones to death before their time." "The ה of <b>המותה</b> — is appended like the ה of <i>lish'olah</i>; the ה is not a feminine marker, and the proof is that the word is mil'eil."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 116, :notes {1 "The Hebrew quotes Numbers 18:16 fragmentarily; translated the sense rather than a specific verse citation, as Ibn Ezra paraphrases."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:52.734062917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}